{"edits": [{"finding_ids": ["app/webhook.py:10:config-class"], "search": "from pydantic import BaseModel", "replace": "from pydantic import BaseModel, ConfigDict, Field", "explanation": "Add ConfigDict and Field imports needed for the v2 model_config and field-level aliases that replace the v1 Config class."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/webhook.py:10:config-class"], "search": "    head_commit_id: str
    repo_name: str
    forced: bool = False

    class Config:
        fields = {
            "head_commit_id": {"alias": "after"},
            "repo_name": {"alias": "repository"},
        }
        allow_population_by_field_name = True", "replace": "    head_commit_id: str = Field(alias="after")
    repo_name: str = Field(alias="repository")
    forced: bool = False

    model_config = ConfigDict(populate_by_name=True)", "explanation": "Pydantic v2 removed the class-based Config and the `fields` option; per-field aliases move to Field(alias=...). The v1 `allow_population_by_field_name = True` becomes `populate_by_name=True` in model_config = ConfigDict(...), so fields are still accepted by alias or by name, as before."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/webhook.py:19:deprecated-method"], "search": "    return GitHubPush.parse_obj(payload)", "replace": "    return GitHubPush.model_validate(payload)", "explanation": "parse_obj is the deprecated v1 classmethod; model_validate is the v2 replacement with the same behavior for a dict payload."}], "notes": "Config class converted to model_config = ConfigDict(populate_by_name=True). The v1 `fields` dict is replaced by per-field Field(alias=...), since v2 no longer accepts it in config. Behavior is preserved: payloads can still use the aliases "after" and "repository", and field names are still accepted. parse_obj is replaced with model_validate. No migration documentation was retrieved, so these changes rely on the standard Pydantic v2 API. Edits do not overlap. I did not change parse_push's signature or anything else."}
